  "findings": [
    "SymPy issue7221 original body requests ordinary proper-rational decomposition and optional shortest-among-methods output; its20 returned comments discuss resource blowup and output tests, not a specified exact-marker request. This is historical public demand, not evidence of a current unresolved feature.",
    "Issue metadata comments=10 differs from the20 returned comment objects. Both response SHAs retained; do not claim a complete issue history or silently replace either count.",
    "Eppstein author-hosted1086-line Python file actually inspected at1-145,700-750,810-1086: constraint predicate, default greedy search, filters, full option definitions and interfaces. Default named greedy enumerates possible denominators; it is not just the one-path Sylvester algorithm.",
    "Eppstein options include length, min/maxdenominator, parity, squares, repeats and enumeration/minimization filters. The inspected option definitions do not expose a required-marker option. The subroutine contains keywords.iteritems(); compatibility was not executed or repaired. No blanket claim about all other methods or software versions.",
    "Martin-Shi2025 author PDF23pages: selected1-2,6-7(Theorem3.2),13-18(selected UFRAC/KILL/early-stop/implementation interfaces),19-20(selected reported costs),21-22(second-largest application). Not a full proof or runtime audit; two actual formula/contract pages7and22 visually checked.",
    "The selected old finite-multiset algorithm returns representations from a finite allowed multiset, with an early-stop variant; a distinct input set is needed for distinct denominators. Finite search and unrestricted short expansion are different output contracts.",
    "A real published mathematical-software caller asks for prescribed second-largest d and largest c*d, with residual target1-1/d-1/(c*d) and bounded remaining denominators. Current pinned Scheme caller sld actually reserves both and calls ufrac-dfs on a constrained range. This establishes related public computational use, not an engineering deployment or an eligible caller for the current single-marker-only APP contract.",
    "Pinned dense-egyptian commit30a3915: full selected files read: README.md=246lines, LICENSE.txt=21lines, u_frac.py=104lines, ufrac-conjecture.scm=35lines, ufrac.scm=256lines. Transitive Scheme math/branch/multithread/prime modules and witnesses were not downloaded or audited; no full software proof/compatibility claim.",
    "Python wrapper actually spawns chez and loads compiled ufrac.so; it is not a standalone Python implementation. No scheme/chez/chezscheme/racket/guile command on current PATH and no SymPy in inspected Python3.12.14 or3.14.8. No install, execution, upstream tests or benchmark; old published timings are author reports, not measured here.",
    "Existing source-guided small-tail prefix does not guarantee two markers, a specified second-largest rank, a finite allowed set, shortest output or maximum denominator. A smaller positive tail excludes reserved reciprocals but can introduce larger denominators, conflicting with rank constraints.",
    "Stop the bounded three-project/source qualification here. Retain APP02501 pending, lower immediate implementation priority; original prediction, conditional-v2 plan, empty run IDs, theory grade and initial-check count unchanged. No global absence inference and no formal rejection."
  ],
